<scaffold_edit_contract>
Rules:
- Input: skeleton, editablePaths, todoToken, outputFormat, repairs.
- Output: ONLY { "edits": [{ "op": "set"|"push"|"removeAt", "path": string, "value"?: any, "index"?: number }] }.
- Each edit.path must match editablePaths EXACTLY (no new paths).
- Do not change structure.

Op rules:
- op="set": only when current value at path in skeleton is exactly todoToken.
- op="push": only when current value at path is an array (including empty).
- op="removeAt": only when current value at path is an array; remove exactly one element at the given zero-based index without reordering other elements.

Repairs (highest priority):
- If repairs is non-empty, you MUST satisfy every repair.
- TODO repair: replace todoToken at that path with a concrete value grounded in context/strategy.
- Missing secondary keyword repair: place that exact keyword ONCE by op="push" into the single best sections.*.keywords array.
  - Never change/remove existing primary keywords in skeleton.
  - Do not place the same secondary keyword in multiple sections.
- If a repair explicitly requires removing an item from an array, use op="removeAt" on that array path with the correct index.

Value rules:
- op="push": value may be one item or an array of items to append.
</scaffold_edit_contract>
